  "handbook-races-title": "Races and abilities",
  "handbook-races-text": "<strong>Race Framework, RF Mechanics and Diet Setup</strong>\nRace Framework supplies racial traits and class availability for character models. Your class adds its own traits. RF Mechanics supplies abilities and ongoing effects. Diet Setup separately controls food responses and nutrition; race diets require matching server-configured bindings.\n\nCharacter creation lists fixed trait modifiers. This page explains the active and passive abilities each race adds beyond those. World configuration, equipment, class and other mods can change a result.\n\n<strong>Controls</strong>\nRace Ability defaults to R. For Dwarves it remains Ore-Song; for Goblins it remains repair spit. Race Stance defaults to Ctrl+H and routes by your race: Dwarf Stonebrace, Elf Watchfulness, Orc Hunt or Goblin Clamber. Existing bindings are preserved; check Settings &gt; Controls if a key differs or conflicts.\n\n<strong>Human</strong>\nYour body follows a familiar human hunger rhythm. You have no race-specific active ability. With matching Diet Setup bindings, food from farm and hunt sustains you evenly.\n\n<strong>Dwarf</strong>\nYour sturdy body holds a generous meal. Stone and ore answer your work more readily as you travel into deep ground, and your body bears cold and heavy armor well.\nCtrl+H toggles Stonebrace. It slows your movement and resists knockback; it only reduces physical attacks. It does not protect you from falls, fire, poison, starvation or other environmental harm. Its protection grows with depth and close stone, then fades after you leave those conditions.\nR remains Ore-Song. Sit still on the ground with an empty main hand, face reachable stone or ore, and press it to listen for broad mineral clues. Stonebrace does not replace Ore-Song.\nWith matching Diet Setup bindings, well-kept food, roots, mushrooms and alcohol suit you best. Fresh fruit and leaves offer less.\n\n<strong>Elf</strong>\nYour light frame needs little food and has a smaller stomach to match. You are suited to foraging and ranged combat; you climb living tree trunks like ladders, pass through branchy leaves freely, and move faster near living trees. You can also step up two-block ledges without jumping. Hold Race Ability to focus your vision, and use Race Stance to toggle Watchfulness for occasional cues from visible movement.\nWith matching Diet Setup bindings, fresh fare, juice, seeds and nuts nourish you well. Meat is left uneaten, fish remains useful, and dairy can fill your stomach without supporting nutrition. As food turns, its virtue fades; preserved food sits badly.\n\n<strong>Orc</strong>\nYour powerful body stores much food and burns through it quickly. Hunt is your Race Stance: it draws the air for scent, sharper while you stand still, and it can reveal blood from creatures wounded nearby as long as they stay out of water. Closing in on a bleeding target on foot quickens your pace. Thew is a bodily reserve sustained by plentiful food and adequate protein or dairy nutrition; hunger depletes it, and it also quietly funds two things: slow healing when you are badly hurt, and a burst of pace and jump while you keep moving hungry. Thick skin is passive.\nWith matching Diet Setup bindings, meat and offal suit you, especially cooked meat. Fruit, leaves and roots barely fill you; the Stats screen does not count their categories as supported.\n\n<strong>Goblin</strong>\nYour small body fills quickly and hungers sooner. Press R to use stored repair spit on an eligible damaged placed block. Literal rot can replenish that spit and strengthen your rot aura; carrying rot or eating partly spoiled food does not activate that signal.\nCtrl+H toggles Clamber. With both hands free you climb eligible walls freely; with a hand occupied you climb more slowly; with neither hand free you cannot hold a wall. Ladders remain usable. You also move faster through earthen tunnels, though stone mining is much slower for you, and crops near your lingering rot aura stop growing until you leave, then recover; they are never destroyed.\nIn darkness, when you carry no light, drifters, shivers and bowtorn notice you much later. Crouching on the ground hides you best, then climbing a wall with both hands free; standing, walking or climbing with one hand is middling, and sprinting is easiest to spot. Bears, hyenas and wolves notice you only a little later, whatever you do. Daylight, a held light, coming within a couple of blocks, or a creature already hunting you reveals you as normal.\nWith matching Diet Setup bindings, literal rot, insects and ageing meat or fish bring out the most in you. Fresh fruit, leaves and roots sit badly, and fresh meat fills you but gives little nourishment.\n\n<strong>Half-Giant</strong>\nYour enormous body holds vast meals but burns through them quickly. You wade through shallow water more easily than most races and only need to swim once it gets deep, and you can step up two-block ledges without jumping. In Survival, your picking reach extends to about 9 blocks, roughly double the usual; it does not change melee reach. With an empty active hand, you can quarry natural rock more quickly. Successful non-creative quarrying keeps normal drops and costs satiety; tools, ore and worked stone do not receive this quarry benefit.\nWith an empty offhand, press R while looking at an animal smaller than a bear, or at a drifter within arm's reach, to carry it; press R while looking at clear ground to release it. With it in your main hand (press X to swap hands), hold right-click and let go for a quick throw, or hold it longer to fully charge a much stronger throw; smaller creatures fly further either way. Your main hand stays free. Drops and transfers preserve the carried animal, but only a Half-Giant can release it. With nothing carried and an empty main hand, press R while looking at an edge or corner of natural rock to pull one rock loose; throw it the same way, and it breaks into stones where it lands. Pulling costs satiety like quarrying. With matching Diet Setup bindings, dairy and grain nourish you well, while roots give a little more.\n\n<strong>Diet Setup</strong>\nEach diet sentence above describes a candidate diet only when the server has configured matching race bindings; the examples are not enabled by this handbook. Food tags, recipe ingredients, freshness and the winning rule decide how food fills you and helps your nutrition. An assigned diet overrides race bindings. A resolved serving that would give your body nothing is left uneaten. When a useful mouthful can provide only a very small fraction, you receive a restrained notice. The Stats screen shows the categories your diet supports.\nSee <a href=\"handbook://dietsetup:diet-guide\">Diet &amp; Nutrition</a> when Diet Setup is installed, or use /dietdiag to check your assigned diet."
}
